WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.269
"Risks and Benefits of
Nicotinic Acid (NA), a NAD+ Booster"

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.680
The name nicotinic acid was
changed to niacin in the 1940s

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.360
to avoid any confusion
with nicotine.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.600
Either name has to be better
than the original moniker, though:

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.640
vitamin PP
(for pellagra preventing).

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.600
In the 1950s, NA became the world’s
first cholesterol-lowering drug.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.280
This led to more than 20 trials involving
tens of thousands of individuals

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.760
taking high doses of
NA for up to six years,

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.200
resulting in by far the most
robust safety data we have

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.640
on any of the NAD+ precursors.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.800
The most striking benefit was found
in the Coronary Drug Project,

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.640
a trial carried out in the pre-statin
drug era of the 1960s and 70s.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.600
The 15-year follow-up found that
those who had been randomized

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.600
to years of high-dose NA ended up
with a 6.2% drop in absolute mortality

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.920
(52% had died in the NA group
versus 58% in the placebo group).

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.440
This sparked major clinical trials that,
sadly, failed so spectacularly

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.560
that one was even
stopped prematurely.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.720
All in all, a Cochrane meta-
analysis concluded that

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.640
“no evidence of benefits from
niacin therapy” was found.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.560
One possible explanation
for the contrasting results

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.080
is that the early promising trials
used immediate release niacin,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.280
while the newer failed trials
used slow release formulations

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.200
(also known as extended
or sustained release).

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.440
At high doses, regular niacin commonly
causes an intense flushing redness

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.720
and prickly heat sensation similar
to a menopausal hot flash.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.640
A slow release version was developed
to reduce this flushing reaction,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.560
catapulting it into a billion-
dollar blockbuster drug,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.760
but it simply doesn’t work as
well to lower cholesterol.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.520
The major clinical trial failures led
to the withdrawal of the drug in Europe

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.840
and the removal from
U.S. clinical guidelines

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.480
for cardiovascular
disease prevention.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.120
There still may be a role
for niacin preparations

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.280
in the treatment
of heart disease

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.080
among patients who cannot
tolerate statin drugs,

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.560
but what about use for the
general public as an NAD+ booster?

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.080
There is a series of
rare genetic defects

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.040
that can lead to a condition
called mitochondrial myopathy

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.080
that’s characterized by low NAD+
levels in the blood and muscles.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.160
In 2020, researchers demonstrated
that these levels could be repleted

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.360
with 750 to 1,000 mg
a day of NA,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.560
which led to a significant
improvement in muscle strength.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.920
This was the first and only study to show
improvements in muscle NAD+ levels

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.120
and performance with
any sort of NAD+ booster.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.920
In a control group of individuals
without the genetic defect,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.080
blood levels of NAD+
were raised by NA,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.200
but not muscle levels,

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.440
suggesting that NAD+ levels are
already “topped off” in normal muscles.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.360
As you’ll see, this is a recurring
theme among NAD+ boosters.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.000
We know that large doses of NA
can boost NAD+ levels in human blood,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:08.160
but a corresponding increase in sirtuin
activity has yet to be demonstrated.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.000
Why not give it a try?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.480
Because of the side effects unearthed
in the cholesterol-lowering trials.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.720
NA raises blood sugars and may increase
your risk of developing diabetes.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.840
Based on studies of tens of thousands
of people on high-dose NA

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.600
who were followed for years,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.800
one would expect that 1 in 43
people taking NA for five years

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.360
would develop diabetes who
otherwise wouldn’t have.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.640
It’s unclear if this risk is only limited
to slow release formulations.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.240
The safety buffer, the ratio between
the tolerable upper limit and the RDA,

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.880
is the lowest for NA compared to
half a dozen other common vitamins.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.920
However, the upper limit is just
based on the flushing reaction,

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.440
which although uncomfortable,
is considered harmless

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.200
and tends to dissipate over time.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.320
Long-term use can have other
adverse consequences, though,

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.800
including stomach ulcers,
vomiting, abdominal pain,

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.000
diarrhea, and jaundice,
a sign of liver toxicity,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.720
which is worse with
slow-release formulations.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.640
There is also a theoretical concern
that excessive NA intake

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.600
may contribute to the development
of Parkinson’s disease.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.040
Due to the unpleasant flushing and
risk of more serious side effects,

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:22.171
interest has moved towards
other NAD+ enhancers.

